course: dictionary
lesson: 8015
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Referee is one of them. «The referee blew the whistle to start the match» is about a person in a game, so a referee is the person who makes sure players follow the rules.
explain: Referee can also be a verb. «The referee gave a yellow card» is about a game, but «to referee an argument» means to help people sort it out fairly. Read the words around the word first, then decide which meaning fits.
explain: Look for clues. Whistles, cards and matches tell you it is about sport. Arguments, siblings and fairness tell you it may be about helping people. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: A referee is the person who makes sure players follow the rules and decides what happens when they do not.
fact: «The referee's word is final: a yellow card is a warning, a red card sends a player off.»
fact: To referee means to act as the referee in a game, or to help people sort out an argument fairly.
fact: A referee can also be a person who writes to say you are good for a job or a school place.
exercise: «The referee blew the whistle.» What is a referee? | A line painted on the pitch | *The person who makes sure players follow the rules | The coach who picks the team | A player who scores the most goals
exercise: «The referee's word is final: a yellow card is a warning, a red card sends a player off.» What does a yellow card mean? | *A warning | A goal for the other team | A player sent off the pitch | A new player coming on
exercise: Sam says a parent can referee a fight between siblings. What does referee mean here? | To run very fast around the garden | To write a letter saying a child is good for a school place | *To help people sort out an argument fairly | To blow a whistle and give out cards
test: Mrs Lee agreed to be my referee for the school place. What does referee mean? | *A person who writes to say you are good for a school place | A player who kicks the ball | A cup given to the winner | A person who blows the whistle
test: What does «to referee» mean in «The club asked Ana to referee the match»? | To sit on the bench and watch | To write a letter about a player | To kick the ball into the net | *To act as the referee in a game
exam: In boxing clubs, coaches teach that skills are only for the ring, with rules and a referee. What does a referee do there? | *Makes sure the fighters follow the rules | Cooks the food for the crowd | Sells the tickets at the door | Teaches the boxers how to punch
